   "title": "First geometry (read me)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Your first procedural model: a tapered tower built from one box.\n\n1) Box makes a 2 x 1 x 2 block; Transform turns it 15 degrees around Y.\n2) Group Create puts the faces whose normal points up (Y, within 10 degrees) into the group 'top'. PolyExtrude #1 takes only that face, insets it and pushes it up. The new top face lands in the group 'extrudeFront'.\n3) PolyExtrude #2 does the same again on 'extrudeFront': a second, narrower storey.\n4) PolyBevel rounds every edge; Color paints the result.\n5) Preview Image (PCG) renders a picture (shown by ComfyUI's Preview Image); 3D Viewport shows the mesh interactively.\n\nTweak: the extrude Distance / Inset, the bevel Distance and Divisions, or switch Preview shading to 'normal' or 'lambert'."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
